IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `crp-rules`

-- Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA) -- the questions of the claimant in a class action in the
-- Supreme Court of Western Australia: a group member, or a person with a claim who starts or runs the class action as
-- the representative party.
--
-- Based on content from the Western Australian Legislation website: "Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act
-- 2022", with "Rules of the Supreme Court 1971" Order 18A and "Interpretation Act 1984" ss 61, 62, State of Western
-- Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public
-- use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts only. What the Court decides (whether it is satisfied, thinks it just, finds an issue
-- common) is asked as a fact: "if the Court ...". A yes about the Court means the Court can do it, not that it will.

§ `Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 -- my questions in a class action`

§§ `Can my claim be in a class action? (ss 2, 4, 6, 7, 10)`

@export Can my claim be brought in a class action (a "representative proceeding") in the Supreme Court of Western Australia under the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA) (ss 4, 6, 10)? Needs 7 or more people with claims against the same person, arising from the same, similar or related circumstances, with a substantial common issue; the Act's Part 2 has been in operation since 25 March 2023, and the cause of action may have accrued at any time.
GIVEN `the day it is commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what day was (or will) the class action be commenced (ISO date, e.g. 2025-03-15)?
      `how many of us have claims` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people, counting you, have claims against the same person (company, government or individual)?
      `our claims share circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the claims arise out of, or concern, the same, similar or related circumstances?
      `our claims share a substantial issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the claims raise a substantial common issue of law or fact (for example whether the product was defective or the statement misleading)?
      `the Court's only jurisdiction is cross-vesting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the Supreme Court have jurisdiction over every claim only because of the cross-vesting laws (Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 or an equivalent)? Answer no if unsure.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my claim be brought in a class action?` `the day it is commenced` `how many of us have claims` `our claims share circumstances` `our claims share a substantial issue` `the Court's only jurisdiction is cross-vesting` MEANS
    `ss 6, 10 -- the claims can be brought as a representative proceeding` `the day it is commenced` `how many of us have claims` `our claims share circumstances` `our claims share a substantial issue` `the Court's only jurisdiction is cross-vesting`

@export Can I start the class action myself, as the representative party, for the others with claims (ss 6, 7(1) of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA), Rules of the Supreme Court 1971 O. 18A r. 2)? You must act through a lawyer. Not answered where you could not sue on your own behalf, which the Act does not settle.
GIVEN `the day it is commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what day was (or will) the class action be commenced (ISO date)?
      `how many of us have claims` IS A NUMBER @desc How many people, counting you, have claims against the same person?
      `our claims share circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the claims arise out of the same, similar or related circumstances?
      `our claims share a substantial issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the claims raise a substantial common issue of law or fact?
      `the Court's only jurisdiction is cross-vesting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would the Supreme Court have jurisdiction over every claim only because of the cross-vesting laws?
      `I could sue on my own` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have a sufficient interest to sue that person on your own behalf (normally yes, if you have a claim against them yourself)?
      `I have a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you commence and run the class action through a legal practitioner (lawyer)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I start the class action as representative party?` `the day it is commenced` `how many of us have claims` `our claims share circumstances` `our claims share a substantial issue` `the Court's only jurisdiction is cross-vesting` `I could sue on my own` `I have a lawyer` MEANS
    `both`
        (`ss 6, 10 -- the claims can be brought as a representative proceeding` `the day it is commenced` `how many of us have claims` `our claims share circumstances` `our claims share a substantial issue` `the Court's only jurisdiction is cross-vesting`)
        (`both` (`s 7(1) -- I have standing to commence` `I could sue on my own`) (`O. 18A r. 2 -- I can commence or carry it on as I act` `I have a lawyer`))

-- Situation: only for the person who started the class action.
@export If I started the class action, can I keep running it and appeal from a decision in it even after my own claim against the respondent ends, for example because I settled (s 7(3) of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))?
GIVEN `I started it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commence the class action yourself (rather than being substituted in later as representative party)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I keep running the class action without a claim of my own?` `I started it` MEANS
    `s 7(3) -- I keep my standing without a claim` `I started it`

§§ `Am I in the group? (ss 3, 8, 9)`

@export Am I a group member in this class action (ss 3, 8 of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? An individual or company described in the group is in it without consenting; the Commonwealth, a State or Territory, a Minister, a public-purpose statutory body or an official acting as such is in only with written consent (Form 10A).
GIVEN `the group described includes me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the description of the group in the application starting the class action (or as amended) cover you? You need not be named.
      `what I am` IS A `Kind of person` @desc Which are you? Most people and companies choose "an individual or a company or other person not listed".
      `I consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you given written consent to be a group member (Form 10A, filed and served on the representative party)? Only matters for the government bodies and officials listed.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I a group member?` `the group described includes me` `what I am` `I consented in writing` MEANS
    `ss 3, 8 -- I am a group member` `the group described includes me` `what I am` `I consented in writing`

@export Do I have to consent to be a group member in a class action (s 8 of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? Only the Commonwealth, a State or Territory, a Minister, a public-purpose statutory body or an official acting as such must consent, in writing.
GIVEN `what I am` IS A `Kind of person` @desc Which are you? Most people and companies choose "an individual or a company or other person not listed".
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must I consent to be a group member?` `what I am` MEANS
    `s 8(2) -- consent in writing is needed` `what I am`

-- Situation: only for a group member under a legal disability (a child, or a person who cannot manage their affairs).
@export Do I need a next friend (a litigation representative) to be a group member, or to take a step in the class action myself, while I am under a legal disability (s 9 of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))?
GIVEN `I am under disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a person the court rules allow to bring a proceeding only by a next friend (for example a child, or a person who cannot manage their own affairs)?
      `what I want to do` IS A `What I want to do` @desc Do you just want to be a group member, or to take a step in the proceeding or conduct part of it?
      `the Court ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered that you may take steps without a next friend?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do I need a next friend?` `I am under disability` `what I want to do` `the Court ordered otherwise` MEANS
    `s 9 -- I need a next friend` `I am under disability` `what I want to do` `the Court ordered otherwise`

§§ `Opting out (ss 12, 13, 29, 30(4))`

@export Can I opt out of the class action by filing notice on this day (s 12 of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA), Rules of the Supreme Court 1971 O. 18A r. 5)? The notice is a Form 10B, filed before the opt-out date the Court fixed: on that date itself is too late. There is no opt-out from an appeal.
GIVEN `the opt-out date` IS A DATE @desc What is the opt-out date the Court fixed (or extended to) in the notice you received (ISO date)? Notice must be given before it.
      `the day I file notice` IS A DATE @desc On what day will you file (or did you file) your opt-out notice (ISO date)?
      `my notice is a filed Form 10B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your notice in writing, as a Form 10B filed with the Supreme Court?
      `this is an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding you want to leave an appeal from the class action's judgment, rather than the class action itself?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I opt out of the class action?` `the opt-out date` `the day I file notice` `my notice is a filed Form 10B` `this is an appeal` MEANS
    `s 12(2) -- I can opt out` `the opt-out date` `the day I file notice` `my notice is a filed Form 10B` `this is an appeal`

@export What is the last day I can file my opt-out notice in the class action (s 12(2) of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? The day before the opt-out date the Court fixed, since notice must be given "before" that date.
GIVEN `the opt-out date` IS A DATE @desc What is the opt-out date the Court fixed (or extended to) (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I opt out?` `the opt-out date` MEANS
    `s 12(2) -- the last day to opt out` `the opt-out date`

@export Can the hearing of the class action start on this day, before I have had the chance to opt out (s 12(4) of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? Not earlier than the opt-out date, unless the Court gives leave.
GIVEN `the hearing day` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the hearing to start (ISO date)?
      `the opt-out date` IS A DATE @desc What is the opt-out date the Court fixed (ISO date)?
      `the Court gave leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court given leave for the hearing to start earlier?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the hearing start before my opt-out date?` `the hearing day` `the opt-out date` `the Court gave leave` MEANS
    `s 12(4) -- the hearing can start then` `the hearing day` `the opt-out date` `the Court gave leave`

-- Situation: only for a person whose claim arose after the class action began.
@export My claim arose after the class action began. Can the Court let the group be widened to include me (s 13 of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? Only if the claim accrued after the class action began and before the date the Court fixes, and you would otherwise have been in the group; the representative party must apply.
GIVEN `the day my claim arose` IS A DATE @desc On what day did your cause of action accrue (ISO date)?
      `the day the class action began` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the class action commenced (ISO date)?
      `the date the Court fixes` IS A DATE @desc What cut-off date has the Court fixed (or been asked to fix) in giving leave to widen the group (ISO date)?
      `I would have been in the group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had your claim accrued before the class action began, would you have been in the group (with your consent, if you are a government body or official)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the group be widened to include my later claim?` `the day my claim arose` `the day the class action began` `the date the Court fixes` `I would have been in the group` MEANS
    `s 13 -- the group can be altered to include me` `the day my claim arose` `the day the class action began` `the date the Court fixes` `I would have been in the group`

§§ `My time limit (s 32)`

@export What happens to the time limit (limitation period) for my own claim while I am in the class action (s 32 of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? It stops running when the class action starts and runs again only if I opt out, or the class action and its appeals end without finally deciding my claim; this gives the new last day.
GIVEN `my claim is in the class action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim one of the group members' claims the class action is about?
      `my old last day` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day to sue on your claim under the limitation law that applies, before the class action (ISO date)?
      `the day the class action began` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the class action commenced (ISO date)?
      `where my claim stands` IS A `Where my claim stands` @desc Is the class action still going, did you opt out, did it (and its appeals) end without finally deciding your claim, or was your claim finally decided in it?
      `the day that happened` IS A DATE @desc On what day did you opt out, or did the class action and its appeals end (ISO date)? Ignored if it is still going.
GIVETH A `Limitation answer`
`What happens to my time limit?` `my claim is in the class action` `my old last day` `the day the class action began` `where my claim stands` `the day that happened` MEANS
    `s 32 -- my limitation period` `my claim is in the class action` `my old last day` `the day the class action began` `where my claim stands` `the day that happened`

§§ `Notices (ss 25, 26)`

@export Must I, as a group member, be given notice of this in the class action (s 25 of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? Notice must be given as soon as practicable after the event, in the form the Court approves and the way it orders.
GIVEN `what it is about` IS A `What the notice is about` @desc What is the notice about?
      `damages are claimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the class action claim damages?
      `the Court dispensed with notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court dispensed with giving this notice?
      `the Court ordered notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered that notice of it be given to group members?
      `the Court thinks it just to go ahead without notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a settlement approval only: is the Court satisfied it is just to decide the application without notice to group members?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I be given notice of this?` `what it is about` `damages are claimed` `the Court dispensed with notice` `the Court ordered notice` `the Court thinks it just to go ahead without notice` MEANS
    `s 25 -- I must be given notice` `what it is about` `damages are claimed` `the Court dispensed with notice` `the Court ordered notice` `the Court thinks it just to go ahead without notice`

@export Can the Court order that notice be given personally to each group member, rather than by advertisement or other means (s 26(4) of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? Only if it is satisfied that is reasonably practicable and not unduly expensive.
GIVEN `the Court finds it practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied that giving notice personally to each group member is reasonably practicable?
      `the Court finds it not unduly expensive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied that doing so is not unduly expensive?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Court order personal notice to each of us?` `the Court finds it practicable` `the Court finds it not unduly expensive` MEANS
    `s 26(4) -- personal notice to each of us can be ordered` `the Court finds it practicable` `the Court finds it not unduly expensive`

@export If I did not receive, or did not respond to, a notice in the class action, does that undo a step taken, an order made or a judgment given (s 26(7) of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? No.
GIVEN `I missed a notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to receive, or fail to respond to, a notice in the class action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does missing a notice affect the class action?` `I missed a notice` MEANS
    `s 26(7) -- my missing a notice affects the proceeding` `I missed a notice`

§§ `The representative party (ss 21, 24)`

@export Can the Court replace the representative party (or a subgroup representative party) on my application, because they cannot adequately represent us or it is otherwise in the interests of justice (s 21 of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? Only a group member can apply to replace the representative party, and only a member of the subgroup to replace its representative.
GIVEN `whom I want replaced` IS A `Whom I want replaced` @desc Do you want the representative party replaced, or a subgroup representative party?
      `I am a group member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a group member in the class action?
      `I am in that subgroup` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a subgroup representative only: are you a member of that subgroup?
      `the Court finds them inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Court that they are not able to adequately represent the group's (or subgroup's) interests?
      `the Court finds it otherwise just` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Court that replacing them is otherwise in the interests of justice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the representative party be replaced on my application?` `whom I want replaced` `I am a group member` `I am in that subgroup` `the Court finds them inadequate` `the Court finds it otherwise just` MEANS
    `s 21 -- the representative can be replaced on my application` `whom I want replaced` `I am a group member` `I am in that subgroup` `the Court finds them inadequate` `the Court finds it otherwise just`

@export Can the Court let the representative party withdraw after settling their own claim (s 24 of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? Only once group members have had notice in time to apply for a substitute, and any such application has been decided.
GIVEN `they are settling their own claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the representative party seeking leave to settle, or has it settled, its own individual claim?
      `we had notice in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied that group members were given notice of the withdrawal application under Part 3, in time to apply to have someone else substituted?
      `substitution applications are decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has every application to substitute another group member as representative party been decided (answer yes if there were none)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the representative party withdraw?` `they are settling their own claim` `we had notice in time` `substitution applications are decided` MEANS
    `s 24 -- the representative can be let withdraw` `they are settling their own claim` `we had notice in time` `substitution applications are decided`

§§ `Stopping the class action (ss 14, 15, 16, 17)`

@export Can the Court order that the class action no longer continue as a class action (ss 14, 15, 16 of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? It can if fewer than 7 group members seem likely, if paying out money to group members would cost the respondent too much, or if the Court is satisfied a class action is not in the interests of justice for a reason in s 16.
GIVEN `group members the Court thinks likely` IS A NUMBER @desc How many group members does it appear likely to the Court that there are?
      `money is claimed for group members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the class action claim payment of money to group members (other than costs)?
      `distribution would cost too much` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court concluded, on the respondent's application, that identifying group members and paying them would cost the respondent too much compared with the likely total?
      `the Court finds a class action unjust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied it is in the interests of justice to end the class action, because of costs, other means of relief, inefficiency or other inappropriateness (s 16)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the class action be stopped?` `group members the Court thinks likely` `money is claimed for group members` `distribution would cost too much` `the Court finds a class action unjust` MEANS
    `ss 14, 15, 16 -- the Court can stop the representative proceeding` `group members the Court thinks likely` `money is claimed for group members` `distribution would cost too much` `the Court finds a class action unjust`

-- Situation: only after the Court has ordered that the proceeding no longer continue as a class action.
@export After the Court ordered that the class action no longer continue as one, can I go on with my own claim in that proceeding (s 17 of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? The representative party may continue on their own behalf; a former group member may apply to be joined as an applicant.
GIVEN `the Court ordered it no longer continue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered, under Part 2 of the Act, that the proceeding no longer continue as a class action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I go on with my own claim after the class action stops?` `the Court ordered it no longer continue` MEANS
    `s 17 -- I can go on with my own claim in it` `the Court ordered it no longer continue`

§§ `Costs (ss 18, 19, 31, 33)`

@export Can the Court order me to pay these costs in the class action (ss 18(3), 19(2), 31 of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? A group member who is not a party cannot be ordered to pay costs, except the costs of an issue about their own claim they were permitted to argue, or as a subgroup representative for the subgroup's issues.
GIVEN `my part` IS A `My part in the class action` @desc What is your part in the class action?
      `which costs` IS A `Kind of costs` @desc Which costs are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be ordered to pay costs?` `my part` `which costs` MEANS
    `s 31 -- costs can be awarded against me` `my part` `which costs`

@export What is the most of the damages awarded in the class action that the Court can order paid to the representative party to cover their costs (s 33 of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? Up to the amount by which their reasonable costs exceed what they can recover from the respondent, and never more than the damages; 0 if there is no award of damages or no application.
GIVEN `damages were awarded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court made an award of damages in the class action?
      `the representative applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the representative party (or a subgroup representative, or a former one) applied under s 33?
      `their reasonable costs` IS A NUMBER @desc In dollars: the costs the Court accepts the applicant reasonably incurred in the class action.
      `their recoverable costs` IS A NUMBER @desc In dollars: the costs the applicant is likely to recover from the respondent.
      `the damages awarded` IS A NUMBER @desc In dollars: the total damages awarded in the class action.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much of the damages can go to the representative's costs?` `damages were awarded` `the representative applied` `their reasonable costs` `their recoverable costs` `the damages awarded` MEANS
    `s 33 -- the most paid to the representative out of the damages` `damages were awarded` `the representative applied` `their reasonable costs` `their recoverable costs` `the damages awarded`

§§ `Settlement and judgment (ss 22, 23, 25(4), 27, 29)`

@export Can the class action be settled or discontinued (s 23, s 25(4) of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? Only with the Court's approval, and a settlement is not approved without notice to group members unless the Court is satisfied that is just.
GIVEN `the Court approves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court approved (or will it approve) the settlement or discontinuance?
      `we were given notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were group members given notice of the application for approval?
      `the Court thinks it just without notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied it is just to decide the application without notice to group members?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the class action be settled?` `the Court approves` `we were given notice` `the Court thinks it just without notice` MEANS
    `ss 23, 25(4) -- the class action can be settled` `the Court approves` `we were given notice` `the Court thinks it just without notice`

@export Can the Court award damages to the group as one lump sum, without fixing each member's amount (s 27(1)(f), (3) of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? Only if a reasonably accurate assessment of the total can be made, unless the Court is approving a settlement.
GIVEN `this is a settlement approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court approving a settlement, rather than giving judgment after a hearing?
      `the total can be assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can a reasonably accurate assessment be made of the total that group members will be entitled to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can damages be awarded as a lump sum?` `this is a settlement approval` `the total can be assessed` MEANS
    `s 27(3) -- damages can be awarded as a lump sum` `this is a settlement approval` `the total can be assessed`

-- Situation: only for a group member the respondent is suing separately.
@export The respondent has started its own proceeding against me in the Supreme Court. Can the Court hold back (stay execution of) what I am awarded in the class action until that proceeding is decided (s 22 of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))?
GIVEN `the respondent is suing me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the respondent to the class action commenced a proceeding in the Supreme Court against you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my award be held back?` `the respondent is suing me` MEANS
    `s 22 -- my award can be stayed` `the respondent is suing me`

@export Will the judgment in the class action bind me (s 29 of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? It binds every group member it describes, except those who opted out.
GIVEN `the judgment describes me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the judgment describe or otherwise identify you among the group members affected by it?
      `I opted out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you opt out of the class action in time?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Will the judgment bind me?` `the judgment describes me` `I opted out` MEANS
    `s 29 -- the judgment binds me` `the judgment describes me` `I opted out`

§§ `Claiming from a fund (s 28)`

-- Situation: only where the Court has ordered a fund to be set up for distributing money to group members.
@export The Court has ordered a fund for paying group members. What is the earliest day the period for claiming from it (the distribution period) can end (s 28(3)(c) of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? No earlier than 6 months after the day of the order.
GIVEN `the day of the fund order` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Court make the order constituting the fund (ISO date)?
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the earliest end of the distribution period?` `the day of the fund order` MEANS
    `s 28(3)(c) -- the earliest end of the distribution period` `the day of the fund order`

-- Situation: only where the Court has ordered a fund to be set up for distributing money to group members.
@export Can I make a claim for payment out of the class action fund on this day (s 28(3)(c), (4) of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? Yes within the distribution period, the last day included; after it, only if the fund had not been fully paid out by the end of the period and the Court thinks it just.
GIVEN `the day of the fund order` IS A DATE @desc On what day did the Court make the order constituting the fund (ISO date)?
      `the end of the distribution period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the distribution period stated in the Court's order (ISO date)?
      `the day I claim` IS A DATE @desc On what day will you make (or did you make) your claim (ISO date)?
      `fully paid out by the end` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the fund been fully distributed before the end of the distribution period?
      `the Court thinks it just` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a late claim only: does the Court think it just to allow it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I claim from the fund?` `the day of the fund order` `the end of the distribution period` `the day I claim` `fully paid out by the end` `the Court thinks it just` MEANS
    `s 28 -- I can claim from the fund` `the day of the fund order` `the end of the distribution period` `the day I claim` `fully paid out by the end` `the Court thinks it just`

§§ `Appeals (s 30(3))`

-- Situation: only where the representative party has not appealed from the judgment in time.
@export The representative party did not appeal from the class action judgment in time. What is the last day I, as another group member, can appeal for the group (s 30(3) of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? 21 days after the representative's time ends; a last day on a weekend moves to the Monday (public holidays are not counted for you).
GIVEN `the representative's last day` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day for the representative party to appeal under the court rules (ISO date)? Ask the lawyers in the class action if unsure.
GIVETH A DATE
`By when can I appeal for the group?` `the representative's last day` MEANS
    `s 30(3) -- my last day to appeal for the group` `the representative's last day`

-- Situation: only after judgment in the class action.
@export Can I bring an appeal for the group on this day, because the representative party (or subgroup representative) did not appeal in time (s 30(3) of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? Only within the further 21 days after their time ends.
GIVEN `the representative's last day` IS A DATE @desc What was the last day for the representative party to appeal under the court rules (ISO date)?
      `the representative appealed in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the representative party (or subgroup representative party) bring an appeal in time?
      `I am in the group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of the group (or of the subgroup) the appeal would represent?
      `the day I file` IS A DATE @desc On what day will you file (or did you file) the appeal (ISO date)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I appeal for the group?` `the representative's last day` `the representative appealed in time` `I am in the group` `the day I file` MEANS
    `s 30(3) -- I can appeal for the group` `the representative's last day` `the representative appealed in time` `I am in the group` `the day I file`

§§ `Funding the class action (s 36)`

@export Can I (or someone funding my claim) be sued in tort for maintenance or champerty, the old wrongs of backing another person's lawsuit (s 36 of the Civil Procedure (Representative Proceedings) Act 2022 (WA))? No for a claim accruing on or after 25 March 2023, when the torts were abolished; for one accruing earlier the Act leaves it to the old law. Whether a funding contract is illegal or against public policy is not affected.
GIVEN `the day it accrued` IS A DATE @desc On what day would the claim for maintenance or champerty have accrued (ISO date)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I be sued for maintenance or champerty?` `the day it accrued` MEANS
    `s 36 -- I can be sued in tort for maintenance or champerty` `the day it accrued`
